+# Network persona captures
+
+These fixtures are raw TLS ClientHello handshake bodies captured from the
+Chromium 149.0.7827.114 macOS arm64 production SSLClientSocket path. The test
+profile used a 32-byte 0x42 Persona seed and generation 7 for the default
+variant, and generation 8 with the existing Chromium ML-DSA signature feature
+set for the ML-DSA variant.
+
+The random, session ID, key-share material, and GREASE values are preserved as
+captured. Regression tests parse protocol fields and normalize GREASE before
+comparison; they do not require cryptographic random bytes to repeat.
+
+The same catalog records the HTTP/2 SETTINGS order, connection window, pseudo
+header order, and the HTTP/3 SETTINGS order produced by this Chromium build.
+HTTP/2 is checked against exact frame bytes. HTTP/3 and QUIC transport
+parameters are checked by their protocol serializers because the QUIC payload
+is encrypted on the wire. No decrypted or reconstructed QUIC payload is
+labelled as a raw capture.
+
+Persona mode derives separate connection-scoped seeds for TLS extension order,
+HTTP/3 GREASE, and QUIC transport parameter ordering. These seeds never replace
+Chromium's cryptographic randomness for connection IDs, key shares, session
+tokens, or TLS key material.
